      "statement": "Meta (buyer) at OCP 2026: its 51.2T CPO evaluation proved integrated optics viable for high-volume manufacturing, and its next target is a 102.4T CPO/NPO product. It weighs CPO against NPO: both improve density and cut power and cost versus retimed pluggables; CPO carries higher optics supply chain risk, while NPO's modular interposer can foster a broader multi-vendor ecosystem. A design target and evaluation, not a purchase commitment; no vendor is named.",
      "subject_id": "e1"
    },
